<p>That’s it — just those few lines and you’re done.</p>

<p>Actually, the core is only 4 lines of code:</p>

<div class="language-objc highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><table class="rouge-table"><tbody><tr><td class="rouge-gutter gl"><pre class="lineno">1
2
3
4
</pre></td><td class="rouge-code"><pre><span class="n">CABasicAnimation</span> <span class="o">*</span><span class="n">scaleAnimation</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="p">[</span><span class="n">CABasicAnimation</span> <span class="nf">animation</span><span class="p">];</span>
<span class="n">scaleAnimation</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">keyPath</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="s">@"transform.scale.x"</span><span class="p">;</span>
<span class="n">scaleAnimation</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">fromValue</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="err">@</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">1</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="mi">0</span><span class="n">f</span><span class="p">);</span>
<span class="n">scaleAnimation</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">toValue</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="err">@</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">1</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="mi">0</span><span class="n">f</span> <span class="o">*</span> <span class="n">ScreenWidth</span><span class="p">);</span>
</pre></td></tr></tbody></table></code></pre></div></div>

<blockquote>
  <p>The key is <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">scaleAnimation.keyPath = @"transform.scale.x";</code> — here we want to scale along the x-axis.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>The scale value goes from <strong>1 to screen width</strong> — of course, you can control how large the value gets.</p>

<p>If you use <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">@"transform.scale.y"</code>, it scales along the Y-axis.</p>

<p>And if you write <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">@"transform.scale"</code>, it scales on both X and Y — give it a try.</p>

<h1 id="summary">Summary</h1>

<p>The animation technique in this post is scaling via <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">transform.scale.y</code>: scaling the layer from a single point produces the loading effect.</p>

